{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Deep waters</b> — missing a kaf, meaning like deep waters that are cold and clear and no foot tramples them, so is the wisdom and counsel that is in a man's heart — pure and clear." "<b>And a man</b> — after one knows the discernments, he draws the counsel from his heart, meaning he learns it from him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:45.507963191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}